Native Flutter inputs and date/time dialogs replace the original popup framework.
The expense/income selector, rounded keypad and four-column category composition
retain the reference design. Exact decimal text replaces calculator arithmetic;
API catalogs and POST replace device persistence. A manual foreign-currency rate
and a visible posted/scheduled state adapt the form to Monetae's contract.
Categories use the T-502 Material/SVG renderer, never Cashew's PNG catalog.
Optional titles stay empty; no title suggestions, tags, attachments, transfers,
loans, recurrent rules or automatic exchange rate are introduced here.
